# Anti-slop & board-first

Read [`DESIGN.md`](../../DESIGN.md) before changing chrome, boards, or play interaction. Do not invent parallel design tokens.

## Board-first interaction law

- **Moves on the board.** Click pieces, squares, cards, columns — not pew button grids that duplicate board actions.
- **Connect Four:** hover / finger-drag shows held disc above column; tap or release drops. No "Column N" buttons.
- **Chess & checkers:** select piece → highlight legal squares → click destination. Deselect on second click of same piece or non-destination square.
- **Deck-builders:** click card to play; optional single "Play whole hand" shortcut only.
- **SemanticAction** legality still derives from `(G, ctx)` outside JSX; render as highlights on the board, not move menus.

## Forbidden tells (cabinet-specific)

Do not introduce:

- Inter / Geist / Space Grotesk or other default AI font stacks
- Indigo-violet accents, purple-blue gradients, vibecode palettes
- Glass, orbs, blobs, page gradients, hover-lift on chrome
- Identical icon-feature cards, pill eyebrows, sparkle/AI badges
- Generic card-on-card sameness on every surface
- Move-button grids replacing board interaction

## Keep

- Source Sans 3 + Fraunces wordmark; four themes; brand pops from logo
- PlayTable slots (info / board / pew); Kenney CC0 default art
- Quiet chrome; personality in boards and brand mark

Player-facing copy rules: `.cursor/rules/player-facing.mdc`.
